    "chunk_text": "\"Amend the illustrations to section 22(l) of the Bill.\"\n\n1505 1506\n\n\u0dd3\u0d9c\u0dc0 \u0d91\u0db8\u0dca.\u0d92. \u0dc3\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dba\u0dad\u0dd2\n\n2024 \u0db8\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd4 3\n\nTo what have you brought this House today? A mere charade of a passage of a Bill, which all of us know could not have been passed.\n\nSir, I am putting this question not just to the Hon. Members of the Government benches, but also to the country. I tell the people, you all wanted a system change and you are justified in doing that. In two days' time, when a Vote is taken in this House and the Government Members vote to defeat this Vote of No-confidence, you all will yet again be justified for calling for a system\n\nchange. But, do not say that all the 225 Members must be thrown into the Diyawanna Oya. One side of the House, those who vote against this Motion, are the ones who must be thrown into the Diyawanna Oya. They are the ones who close their eyes to what is staring them in the face and will be voting against this Motion. They will be voting with their feet; they will be voting against their own conscience and they will be voting against any sense of reason. That is what I have to say to the country.\n\nI am also addressing the Hon. Speaker. If you have any honour left, please resign. The Mover of this Motion said how the Speaker of the Scottish Parliament admitted his mistake. So, admit your mistake. You do not have to be a legal expert to know what you have done. Admit your mistake, tender your resignation and thereby, guard your honour.\n\nThank you. \u0db4\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dc1\u0dca\u0db1\u0db1\u0dba \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0dd2\u0db8\u0db8\u0dd4\u0d9b \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0db1 \u0dbd\u0daf\u0dd3. \u0bb5\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bc6\u0bbe \u0b8e\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baf\u0bae\u0bcd\u0baa\u0baa\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0baa\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0ba4\u0bc1. Question proposed. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b95\u0bc1\u0bb4\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0bc6\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Chairman of Committees) The next speaker is the Hon. Minister, (Dr.) Wijeyadasa Rajapakshe. You have 30 minutes."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
