    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0b95\u0bb2\u0b95\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) \u0d9c\u0dc0 \u0dba\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0dcf \u0dc4\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0dca\u0db4 \u0dca\u0dd0\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dd4,\u0dca\u0dd2. \u0d94\u0db6\u0dd4,\u0dca\u0dd2\u0da7 \u0dd2\u0db0)\u0dd2\u0dd2 9]\u0da7 \u0da7\u0dd2\u0db1 [ \u0dad\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db6)1\u0dd2.\n\n[1.57 p.m.] \u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0da5 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0db1 \u0dc3\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0ba3\u0bbf \u0bb1\u0bb5\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd \u0bb9\u0b95\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Rauff Hakeem, Attorney-at-Law) Bismillahir Rahmanir Raheem\n\nSir, there are two important components of this No-Confidence Motion. One relates to the conduct of the Speaker during the Committee Stage Amendments of a Bill, the manner in which he refused to consider the valid objections that were raised by the Opposition, which resulted in the Bill being enacted into law totally against or rather contravening certain directions that had been given by the Supreme Court. Then, the other component relates to the conduct of the Speaker in his capacity as the Chairman of the Constitutional Council in interpreting the provisions of the Constitution to suit the whims and fancy of the Executive when it came to the decision to appoint the Inspector General of Police. In both these matters, I would, first of all before we put the blame squarely on the Speaker, point out that both the Attorney-General as well as the Officers of the Parliament Secretariat - the Secretary General and her two assistants - must bear some responsibility. Why do I say that? It is because when such an issue is brought to the notice of the Speaker, it has been the practice in the House and the duty of the officials of Parliament to advise the Speaker\n\n1705 1706\n\n\u0dd3\u0d9c\u0dc0 \u0dda\u0daf \u0d9c\u0dca\u0db4\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0db4\u0dd2\u0db1 \u0dca\u0dc4\u0dba\u0dad\u0dd2\n\n2024 \u0dca\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd4, 20\n\nregarding the alternative methodologies with which we can address that issue. Particularly, it was open to the Speaker to suspend the House temporarily, call for a Party Leaders\u2019 Meeting and summon the Attorney-General\u2019s representative who was in the Officials\u2019 Box, and that was the very request we made."
