    "chunk_size_bytes": 1575,
    "chunk_text": "regarding the alternative methodologies with which we can address that issue. Particularly, it was open to the Speaker to suspend the House temporarily, call for a Party Leaders\u2019 Meeting and summon the Attorney-General\u2019s representative who was in the Officials\u2019 Box, and that was the very request we made.\n\nIn the first instance, when the Legal Draftsman\u2019s Department sent the Bill to the Attorney-General, he certified it as being in conformity with the Constitution and that is how the Cabinet approved the Bill. So, he failed at the first instance and subsequently, he had to face 45 petitions. Then, yesterday, the Minister of Justice was arguing about some Clauses, saying that those Clauses had been accommodated as suggested by the Supreme Court in differently numbered Clauses. But, he admitted that, at least, four of those Clauses had not been in conformity with the Supreme Court\u2019s decision and therefore, the Cabinet has already decided to move amendments to the Bill. That is the very reason why we wanted the Speaker to take that simple decision. This unfortunate situation of moving a No-Confidence Motion would not have come about if the Officers of the Parliament Secretariat at the desk discussed this matter with the Speaker, convinced the Government benches and called for a Party Leaders\u2019 Meeting by suspending the Sitting for a very short while. Then, this whole issue would have been sorted out. Now, we have a Bill which had been enacted into law totally against the Supreme Court's Determination. So, that is one component of this Motion."
