    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "0dad1e2eb267e72c75b2d4e82bdc6fac",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2013,
    "chunk_text": "I recall that at one point, when there was a vote on a Resolution in Geneva, in favour of the Resolution, there was a certain number and against it, there was another number. Then, there were certain other countries which abstained and the Government at that time added the number which abstained to the number of votes they received and said, \u201cWe won the Resolution\u201d. Actually, it was the other way round. The Resolution was brought in by someone else and the Government said, \"We defeated the Resolution\", which was not the case. The United Nations did not accept that position.\n\nWe cannot have a person who had been found guilty of torture in charge of the Police! How could it be? How could it be, Hon. Presiding Member?\n\nIs this not a democracy? Do people not have rights? If those officers have only been accused, that is another matter. You can say that they have only been accused, but not convicted. But, here, it is a conviction. So, purely on that matter, I have lost confidence in the Speaker. I am sorry, I am really sorry to say that; it is not the man, but the position. He wields so much power. We found out during the Debate in this House that the Hon. Speaker did not actually cast his casting vote at the Constitutional Council, he did not. The Hon. Lakshman Kiriella specifically stated that. And, it was much later that he wrote to the Hon. President saying that it was a 5: 4 vote.\n\nSir, there are many other issues that I wish to take up, but I am in no mood to do so because this is not something I enjoy doing; this is something that I do not enjoy doing, but I am doing it because it has to be done.\n\n1867 1868\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014 * \u0db4\u0dd4\u0dca\u0db4\u0dad\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dc0 \u0dad\u0db6\u0dcf \u0d87\u0dad. * \u0ba8\u0bc2\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0ba8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bb2\u0baf\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b95\u0bb5\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bc1. * Placed in the Library.\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1 \u0d9a\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nSo, it is on that basis and many other things that I support this Vote of No Confidence against the Speaker of Parliament."
  },
