    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "7dd3a2b1041268ffbf6364e978bb7ddc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1931,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cThis clause amends section 5 of the principal enactment and the legal effect of the section as amended is to remove the reference to domestic banking business and offshore banking business considering the elimination of the demarcation between domestic banking business and the offshore banking business.\u201d\n\nThen, referring to Clause 17, it is stated, I quote:\n\nSir, the regulatory action in 2023 by the Central Bank requiring businesses operating in the Colombo Port City\u2019s offshore environment to operate through special accounts opened in Domestic Banking Units is intriguing as the ideal platform to operate offshore banking accounts was accounts opened in OBUs under Part IV of the Banking Act. The regulator complicated this landscape and introduced unnecessary risks and uncertainties by opting to permit these accounts under Domestic Banking Units and disregarding the existence of the more suitable offshore banking framework provided in Part IV of the Banking Act. Moreover, the replacement of statutory protections and administrative permissions could deter the current potential foreign entities due to the perceived increase in regulatory risk. This change may prompt a reassessment of the operational viability of banking accounts in Sri Lanka by businesses currently engaged in Offshore Banking Units, potentially leading to capital flight.\n\nTherefore, Sir, I urge this esteemed House to consider this matter. If the proposed Amendments have been meticulously evaluated, it is imperative that the rationale along with the associated risks and benefits of repealing Part IV be transparently deliberated in this Parliament. The legislative process mandates thorough scrutiny of both the intents and implications of such significant Amendments to ensure that they contribute positively to our nation\u2019s financial architecture and long-term economic vision.\n\nThank you.\n\n241 242\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0d9a\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dda\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0"
  },
